      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the FDA-labeled maximum for metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day. Most guidelines recommend staying at or below 2,000 mg/day. Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and include the clinical rationale. I can add it as a note on the order. Otherwise, tell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
